\]

With this formulation and the constraints provided, one may solve for the \( c_i \) coefficients, and then evaluate \( P(6) \).

Please use the initial values \( P(1) + P(2) = 284 \) and \( P(3) + P(4) = 618 \), and \( P(5) = 172 \) to derive a coherent representation of \( P (x) \).
